-- R37 amendment, 25 Nov 2026 (owner, thread "Make USD drivers email easier to read": "Can you do some formatting or
-- coloring to highlight important lines so I know which bits to read"). Replaces point 5 (PHONE ALERT) of the R37 body
-- with points 5 and 5a: the alert goes as HTML (verdict box, trade box, coloured/greyed readings) with a plain-text twin.
-- Run as the single statement below; <owner address> is his Gmail address in the database copy only (public repo).
-- Read back: md5(substr(body,3288,3615)) = ab4a9893081dd32f6f39795cd4e5e6b7, length(body) 4063 -> 7039.
update dash.rules set body = substr(body,1,3287) || $p$5. PHONE ALERT (Fable pipeline only; the Opus pipeline prints the block and sends nothing extra). After the digest email has gone, never before it and never delaying it, send one more Gmail message to <owner address> with subject "USD drivers: <REGIME>" plus " (CHANGED from <yesterday's>)" when it changed. Every day, so his phone shows it; it is a copy of the block, never new analysis. A failed send prints "USD alert: send failed" in the footer and does not retry more than once.
5a. FORMAT (owner's ask 25 Nov 2026: "highlight important lines so I know which bits to read"). Send htmlBody AND body: body = the block as plain text (lines a to g) plus the source line; htmlBody = the layout below, inline styles only, no <style>, no images, under 6 KB. Every number and every line of a to g appears exactly as printed in the digest; the layout only orders, colours and bolds. Fill <...>; drop nothing.
TOP BOX (verdict): <div style="font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;color:#1a1a1a;max-width:640px"><div style="background:<BG>;border-left:6px solid <C>;padding:10px 12px;margin:0 0 10px"><div style="font-size:12px;color:#666">DOLLAR DRIVERS · pack I, <as-of></div><div style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:<C>;margin:2px 0"><REGIME> <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#666">· unchanged</span></div><div style="font-weight:700"><TAKEAWAY></div></div>
  Regime colours <C>/<BG>: FRAGILE #b36b00/#fff4e0; US-ASSET UNWIND #c0392b/#fdecea; RATES-LED and RISK-OFF HEDGE #1e7e34/#e9f7ec; MIXED #555/#f2f2f2. When the regime CHANGED, the span reads "· CHANGED from <yesterday's>" in color:#c0392b instead of "· unchanged". TAKEAWAY = one sentence, at most about 20 words, restating line (e)'s call in its own claims (what carries USD today); no new claim.
TRADE BOX: <div style="background:#eef4ff;border-left:6px solid #2a62c9;padding:10px 12px;margin:0 0 10px"><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:#2a62c9">EXPRESSION (g) · candidate, not a card</div><div><line g text before INVALIDATION, with structure/strikes and r/r in <b></div><div style="margin-top:6px;color:#c0392b"><b>INVALIDATION:</b> <its text></div><div style="margin-top:6px;color:#8e44ad"><b>PAIN TRADE:</b> <pain trade and consensus clause from (e)></div></div>
READINGS: a label <div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:#666;margin:12px 0 4px">THE READINGS</div>, then lines a, b, c, d, e, f always in that order, each as <div style="border-left:4px solid <LC>;padding:4px 10px;margin:0 0 8px<GREY>"><b>(x) NAME</b> <TAG><br><line text></div>, then the source line <div style="font-size:12px;color:#888;margin-top:10px">From: <digest name and date></div></div>.
  SIGNAL line: LC #e08a00, TAG <span style="font-size:12px;color:#b36b00;font-weight:700">· <3-6 word reason></span>, the 1-3 decisive numbers in <b>. Use LC/colour #c0392b instead when the reading argues the regime is turning (hedge broken, sell-America 3+, regime CHANGED). QUIET line: LC #ccc, GREY = ;color:#999, TAG "· quiet", no bold numbers. Line (e) is never greyed (LC #ccc, no TAG); line (f) is a signal when any window cell flips sign against the 1w cell, else quiet.
  Signal tests (from section I numbers): (a) USD 1m and its rate-model part differ in sign, or by more than 1.0pt, for EUR or JPY; (b) |DXY per -1% SPX, 20d| >= 0.10, or sell-America days >= 3; (c) any |residual z| >= 1.5; (d) any CFTC 3y pct >= 85 or <= 15, an R02 or scanner extreme, or |RR25 avg| >= 0.5. Otherwise quiet. Line (f) WINDOWS prints every day (rule 3(f)); its 1d | 3d | 1w rows go one per <br>.

$p$ || substr(body,3927) where rid='R37' and position('5. PHONE ALERT' in body)=3288 and position('6. FOOTER' in body)=3927;
